@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il07-nouns`
IMPORT `il07-refusals`
IMPORT `ito66-nouns`
IMPORT `ito66-tax-years`
IMPORT `ito66-d-common-source`
IMPORT `ito66-a-separate-calculation`
IMPORT `ito66-b-property-income`
IMPORT `ito66-ab-taxable-income`
IMPORT `ito66-c-credit-points`

-- ===========================================================================
-- IL-07 adapter for row IL-02: Income Tax Ordinance s 66, separate calculation.
--
-- Imports this row's nouns and refusals and IL-02's modules, and no other row.
-- It builds IL-02's `Spouses in a tax year` from the household and hands it to
-- IL-02's rules. It exposes booleans, numbers and this row's own record.
--
-- THE COUPLE AS IL-02 SEES IT (input conventions, BRIEF.md "The household"):
-- * the earner's only income is the salary, one item of income from personal
--   exertion of the kind `from employment` (s 66(a)(1)), for the whole year;
-- * the spouse has no income (the pipeline declines otherwise, and so does this
--   adapter, rather than build a spouse whose income it does not know);
-- * no property income under s 66(b), and neither spouse claims under (b);
-- * no common source of income (s 66(d)): a salary from an employer is not
--   "a source of income of one spouse that depends on the other's";
-- * every child is a child of both spouses, so (4A) and (6), which reach only a
--   widowed partner's own children, add nothing; the widowed flags are FALSE;
-- * no child has income within s 66(a)(3).
--
-- VERSION 0.2.0: whether the earner would be entitled to a point under s 37,
-- which IL-02 halves under s 66(c)(2), is no longer read from the couple's
-- record by the pipeline: it passes row IL-08's s 37 answer to the rules below
-- whose names end "..., with a point under section 37:". The rules without that
-- ending read the couple's record as version 0.1.0 did (the tests use them).
--
-- VERSION 0.3.0 (2026-10-08, BACKLOG IL-22). Row IL-02's version 0.2.0 renamed
-- its `A child` to `A child, for section 66` (its 02-N3, so that a module can name
-- it beside row IL-06's) and gave `A spouse` the field `a foreign worker within
-- the meaning of section 48A`, which s 66(c)(4)'s half point under s 36A reads
-- (its 02-R2: a foreign-worker woman is declined in row IL-01's words). The
-- earner's comes from the household's `the earner is a foreign worker`, the fact
-- the IL-01 and IL-08 adapters already pass; the spouse's is a named refusal,
-- never read (il07-refusals.l4). Row IL-02's tax-year gate now wraps every rule
-- that takes the couple; the capstone asks 2026 only, which it answers.
--
-- VERSION 0.5.0 (2026-10-08, BACKLOG IL-54). Row IL-02's version 0.4.0 (SHRUG)
-- adds three facts the adapter must give. INPUT CONVENTIONS (assumed, not ruled:
-- the lead's direction for IL-54):
-- * `an Israeli resident in the tax year, for section 36A` (its fork F20): the
--   earner's is the household's residence fact under the Ordinance, the one the
--   IL-01 adapter passes; the spouse's is a named refusal, never read, as the
--   spouse's foreign-worker fact is (il07-refusals.l4);
-- * of the children's income within (a)(3), the part from inherited assets or
--   from compensation or insurance for bodily injury (its fork F6): 0, since no
--   child has income within (a)(3) (above);
-- * the readings of s 66 to take: NOTHING, that is row IL-02's own switches,
--   each of which declines by default only where its readings part.
-- There is still no common source of income, so the common source's new fact is
-- not given.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `IL-07 adapter — row IL-02`

§§ `The household, as IL-02's spouses in a tax year`

GIVEN `is a woman` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Sex`
`IL-02: the sex` `is a woman` MEANS
    IF `is a woman` THEN `a woman` ELSE `a man`

GIVEN h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      c IS AN `IL-07 couple`
      `s 37` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A spouse`
`IL-02: the earner as a spouse, in` h `married as` c `, with a point under section 37:` `s 37` MEANS
    `A spouse` WITH
        `sex`                                            IS `IL-02: the sex` (e's `the earner is a woman`)
        `income from personal exertion`                  IS LIST (`An item of income from personal exertion` WITH
            `kind`           IS `from employment`
            `taxable amount` IS 12 TIMES e's `the earner's monthly salary`
            `paid in respect of employment income for which the spouse was entitled to a separate calculation` IS FALSE
            `the spouse was entitled to a separate calculation, in the five years before the pension began, for the income by virtue of which it is paid` IS FALSE)
        `taxable income not from personal exertion`      IS 0
        `taxable income from property owned one year before the marriage` IS 0
        `taxable income from property inherited during the marriage`      IS 0
        `claims a separate calculation of the tax on income from personal exertion` IS c's `the earner claims a separate calculation of the tax on the earner's income from personal exertion`
        `claims a separate calculation of the tax on the property income in subsection (b)` IS FALSE
        `a widow or widower when the present marriage was contracted` IS FALSE
        `would be entitled to a credit point under section 37`        IS `s 37`
        `a foreign worker within the meaning of section 48A`          IS e's `the earner is a foreign worker`
        `an Israeli resident in the tax year, for section 36A`        IS e's `the earner was an Israeli resident in the tax year, under the Income Tax Ordinance`
    WHERE
        e MEANS h's `the earner`

GIVEN c IS AN `IL-07 couple`
GIVETH A `A spouse`
`IL-02: the earner's spouse as a spouse, in` c MEANS
    IF   NOT (s's `the spouse's taxable income in the tax year` EQUALS 0)
    THEN `IL-07 composes a household with one earner; a spouse with taxable income is outside it`
    ELSE `A spouse` WITH
             `sex`                                            IS `IL-02: the sex` (s's `the spouse is a woman`)
             `income from personal exertion`                  IS EMPTY
             `taxable income not from personal exertion`      IS 0
             `taxable income from property owned one year before the marriage` IS 0
             `taxable income from property inherited during the marriage`      IS 0
             `claims a separate calculation of the tax on income from personal exertion` IS FALSE
             `claims a separate calculation of the tax on the property income in subsection (b)` IS FALSE
             `a widow or widower when the present marriage was contracted` IS FALSE
             `would be entitled to a credit point under section 37`        IS FALSE
             `a foreign worker within the meaning of section 48A`          IS `IL-07 holds no foreign-worker fact for the earner's spouse, and computes none of the spouse's own credits`
             `an Israeli resident in the tax year, for section 36A`        IS `IL-07 holds no residence fact under the Income Tax Ordinance for the earner's spouse, and computes none of the spouse's own credits`
    WHERE
        s MEANS c's `the earner's spouse`

-- s 40(b)(3), incorporated by s 66(c)(4)(a): "שנת לידה" is the tax year in which
-- the child was born; a tax year is a calendar year (IL-02 NOTES.md A4).
GIVEN k IS AN `IL-07 child`
GIVETH A `A child, for section 66`
`IL-02: the household's child` k MEANS
    `A child, for section 66` WITH
        `tax year of birth`                              IS DATE_YEAR (k's `the child's date of birth`)
        `a child of the registered spouse`               IS TRUE
        `a child of the spouse who is not the registered spouse` IS TRUE
        `the mother elects to count one birth-year credit point in the following tax year` IS k's `the child's mother elects to count one birth-year credit point in the following tax year`
        `taxable income from a transparent company`      IS 0
        `taxable income from a real estate investment trust` IS 0
        `taxable income from interest`                   IS 0
        `taxable income from capital gain`               IS 0

GIVEN h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      c IS AN `IL-07 couple`
GIVETH A `Spouses in a tax year`
`IL-02: the spouses in the tax year, in` h `married as` c MEANS
    `IL-02: the spouses in the tax year, in` h `married as` c `, with a point under section 37:`
        (c's `the earner would be entitled to a credit point under section 37 of the Income Tax Ordinance`)

GIVEN h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      c IS AN `IL-07 couple`
      `s 37` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Spouses in a tax year`
`IL-02: the spouses in the tax year, in` h `married as` c `, with a point under section 37:` `s 37` MEANS
    `IL-02: the spouses in the tax year, in` h `married as` c `, with a point under section 37:` `s 37` `, reading section 66 as` NOTHING

-- Version 0.5.0: the readings of row IL-02's forks for the capstone's readings
-- (il07-nouns.l4): F18 and F20 as the capstone names them, every other fork at
-- row IL-02's own switch.
@ref ITO s 66 (row IL-02 v0.4.0, ito66-nouns.l4, its forks F1, F6, F7, F8, F14, F18, F20)
GIVEN r IS AN `IL-07 the readings of the composed rows' forks`
GIVETH A `Readings of section 66 for a couple`
`IL-02: its readings of section 66, for` r MEANS
    `Readings of section 66 for a couple` WITH
        `F1, where a common source of income fails subsection (d)(1)`                    IS `section 66(d)(1) — the reading this row takes where a common source of income fails its conditions`
        `F6, the exception in section 65 under (a)(3)`                                    IS `section 66(a)(3) — the reading this row takes of the exception in section 65`
        `F14, the children's income under (a)(3) when the pool goes to the other spouse`  IS `section 66(a)(2)-(3) — the reading this row takes of the children's income when the pool goes to the spouse who is not the registered spouse`
        `F7, the proviso to (b) as to the registered spouse`                             IS `section 66(b) — the reading this row takes of the proviso as to the registered spouse`
        `F18, (c)(1A) as to the registered spouse`                                       IS
            CONSIDER r's `section 66(c)(1A) as to the registered spouse (row IL-02 fork F18)`
            WHEN `IL-07: section 66(c)(1A) at row IL-02's switch, declined where the readings differ`         THEN `section 66(c)(1A) — the reading this row takes as to the registered spouse`
            WHEN `IL-07: the registered spouse may request a separate calculation under section 66(c)(1A)`    THEN `the registered spouse may request under (c)(1A)`
            WHEN `IL-07: only the spouse who is not the registered spouse may request under section 66(c)(1A)` THEN `only the spouse who is not the registered spouse may request under (c)(1A)`
        `F8, (c)(1A) where a common source fails (d)(1)`                                 IS `section 66(c)(1A) — the reading this row takes where a common source of income fails subsection (d)(1)`
        `F20, section 36A and residence, under (c)(4)`                                   IS
            CONSIDER r's `section 36A on residence (row IL-01 fork F1, row IL-02 fork F20)`
            WHEN `IL-07: section 36A at the rows' own switches, declined where residence decides it` THEN `section 66(c)(4) — the reading this row takes of section 36A on residence`
            WHEN `IL-07: section 36A without a residence condition`                                  THEN `the half point under section 36A without a residence condition`
            WHEN `IL-07: section 36A only for an Israeli resident`                                   THEN `the half point under section 36A only for an Israeli resident`

GIVEN h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      c IS AN `IL-07 couple`
      `s 37` IS A BOOLEAN
      r IS AN `IL-07 the readings of the composed rows' forks`
GIVETH A `Spouses in a tax year`
`IL-02: the spouses in the tax year, in` h `married as` c `, with a point under section 37:` `s 37` `, reading the composed rows' forks as` r MEANS
    `IL-02: the spouses in the tax year, in` h `married as` c `, with a point under section 37:` `s 37` `, reading section 66 as` (JUST (`IL-02: its readings of section 66, for` r))

GIVEN h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      c IS AN `IL-07 couple`
      `s 37` IS A BOOLEAN
      m IS A MAYBE `Readings of section 66 for a couple`
GIVETH A `Spouses in a tax year`
`IL-02: the spouses in the tax year, in` h `married as` c `, with a point under section 37:` `s 37` `, reading section 66 as` m MEANS
    `Spouses in a tax year` WITH
        `tax year`                                       IS h's `the year of the month`
        `the registered spouse`                          IS IF c's `the earner is the registered spouse` THEN `earner's record` ELSE `other's record`
        `the spouse who is not the registered spouse`    IS IF c's `the earner is the registered spouse` THEN `other's record` ELSE `earner's record`
        `children`                                       IS map `IL-02: the household's child` (h's `the children of the household`)
        `common source of income`                        IS NOTHING
        `of the children's income within (a)(3), the part from assets received by inheritance or from compensation or insurance for bodily injury` IS 0
        `the readings of section 66 to take, if not this row's` IS m
    WHERE
        `earner's record` MEANS `IL-02: the earner as a spouse, in` h `married as` c `, with a point under section 37:` `s 37`
        `other's record`  MEANS `IL-02: the earner's spouse as a spouse, in` c

GIVEN c IS AN `IL-07 couple`
GIVETH A `Which spouse`
`IL-02: which spouse the earner is, in` c MEANS
    IF c's `the earner is the registered spouse` THEN `registered spouse` ELSE `spouse who is not the registered spouse`

§§ `Section 66(c) — whether it governs, and what it gives`

@ref ITO s 66(c) chapeau, (a)(1), (c)(1A) (row IL-02, ito66-c-credit-points.l4)
GIVEN h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      c IS AN `IL-07 couple`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IL-02: section 66(c) governs the earner's calculation, in` h `married as` c MEANS
    `s 66(c) — governs the calculation of the` (`IL-02: which spouse the earner is, in` c) `in` (`IL-02: the spouses in the tax year, in` h `married as` c)

@ref ITO s 66(c) chapeau, (a)(1), (c)(1A) (row IL-02 v0.4.0, ito66-c-credit-points.l4, its fork F18)
GIVEN h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      c IS AN `IL-07 couple`
      r IS AN `IL-07 the readings of the composed rows' forks`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IL-02: section 66(c) governs the earner's calculation, in` h `married as` c `, reading the composed rows' forks as` r MEANS
    `s 66(c) — governs the calculation of the` (`IL-02: which spouse the earner is, in` c) `in`
        (`IL-02: the spouses in the tax year, in` h `married as` c `, with a point under section 37:`
             (c's `the earner would be entitled to a credit point under section 37 of the Income Tax Ordinance`) `, reading the composed rows' forks as` r)

@ref ITO s 66(c) (row IL-02, ito66-c-credit-points.l4)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`IL-02 reports that section 66(c) does not govern the earner's calculation` MEANS
    REFUSE "IL-02 reports that section 66(c) does not govern the earner's calculation"

@ref ITO s 66(c)(2), (4)-(6) (row IL-02, ito66-c-credit-points.l4); IL-02's tax-year gate (ito66-tax-years.l4)
GIVEN h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      c IS AN `IL-07 couple`
GIVETH AN `IL-07 credit points section 66(c) gives the earner`
`IL-02: the credit points section 66(c) gives the earner, in` h `married as` c MEANS
    `IL-02: the credit points section 66(c) gives the earner, in` h `married as` c `, with a point under section 37:`
        (c's `the earner would be entitled to a credit point under section 37 of the Income Tax Ordinance`)

@ref ITO s 66(c)(2), (4)-(6) (row IL-02, ito66-c-credit-points.l4); IL-02's tax-year gate (ito66-tax-years.l4)
GIVEN h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      c IS AN `IL-07 couple`
      `s 37` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `IL-07 credit points section 66(c) gives the earner`
`IL-02: the credit points section 66(c) gives the earner, in` h `married as` c `, with a point under section 37:` `s 37` MEANS
    `IL-02: the points of` (`IL-02: the spouses in the tax year, in` h `married as` c `, with a point under section 37:` `s 37`) `, for the earner in` c

-- Version 0.5.0: the same, at the capstone's readings of row IL-02's forks.
@ref ITO s 66(c)(2), (4)-(6) (row IL-02 v0.4.0, ito66-c-credit-points.l4, its forks F18, F20)
GIVEN h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      c IS AN `IL-07 couple`
      `s 37` IS A BOOLEAN
      r IS AN `IL-07 the readings of the composed rows' forks`
GIVETH AN `IL-07 credit points section 66(c) gives the earner`
`IL-02: the credit points section 66(c) gives the earner, in` h `married as` c `, with a point under section 37:` `s 37` `, reading the composed rows' forks as` r MEANS
    `IL-02: the points of` (`IL-02: the spouses in the tax year, in` h `married as` c `, with a point under section 37:` `s 37` `, reading the composed rows' forks as` r) `, for the earner in` c

-- For the tests: the same, with the s 37 point from the couple's record.
@ref ITO s 66(c)(2), (4)-(6) (row IL-02 v0.4.0, ito66-c-credit-points.l4)
GIVEN h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      c IS AN `IL-07 couple`
      r IS AN `IL-07 the readings of the composed rows' forks`
GIVETH AN `IL-07 credit points section 66(c) gives the earner`
`IL-02: the credit points section 66(c) gives the earner, in` h `married as` c `, reading the composed rows' forks as` r MEANS
    `IL-02: the credit points section 66(c) gives the earner, in` h `married as` c `, with a point under section 37:`
        (c's `the earner would be entitled to a credit point under section 37 of the Income Tax Ordinance`) `, reading the composed rows' forks as` r

@ref ITO s 66(c)(2), (4)-(6) (row IL-02, ito66-c-credit-points.l4)
GIVEN couple IS A `Spouses in a tax year`
      c      IS AN `IL-07 couple`
GIVETH AN `IL-07 credit points section 66(c) gives the earner`
`IL-02: the points of` couple `, for the earner in` c MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 66(c) — the credit points it gives the` (`IL-02: which spouse the earner is, in` c) `in` couple
    WHEN `section 66(c) does not govern the spouse's calculation`
        THEN `IL-02 reports that section 66(c) does not govern the earner's calculation`
    WHEN `in a separate calculation` cp
        THEN `IL-07 credit points section 66(c) gives the earner` WITH
                 `IL-02's half point under section 36A, by section 66(c)(4)` IS cp's `one half point under section 36A, by paragraph (4)`
                 `IL-02's half point under section 37, by section 66(c)(2)`  IS cp's `one half point under section 37, by paragraph (2)`
                 `IL-02's points for children, by section 66(c)(4) to (6)`  IS cp's `points for children, by paragraphs (4), (4A), (5) and (6)`

-- F13 of row IL-02: the children's credit is the lesser of their value and the
-- tax on the spouse's income from personal exertion. (0.5.0: row IL-02's v0.4.0
-- makes F13 a switch; by this old name the rule is at the row's switch, which
-- declines where the value exceeds that tax. The form below names a reading.)
@ref ITO s 66(c)(1A), (4), (5) (row IL-02, ito66-c-credit-points.l4; IL-02 fork F13)
GIVEN `the points for children` IS A NUMBER
      `the value`               IS A NUMBER
      `the tax`                 IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-02: the credit for` `the points for children` `children's points at a value of` `the value` `, set against a tax on income from personal exertion of` `the tax` MEANS
    `s 66(c)(4)-(5) — the credit for children, set against the tax on income from personal exertion:` `the points for children` `,` `the value` `,` `the tax`

-- Version 0.5.0: row IL-02's refusal for its fork F13, for the pipeline's fork
-- K23, which declines in these words where the reading changes the tax.
@ref ITO s 66(c)(1A), (4), (5) (row IL-02 v0.4.0, ito66-c-credit-points.l4; IL-02 fork F13)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`IL-02: the set-off of the children's credit is not decided` MEANS
    `section 66(c)(4)-(5) do not say whether the children's credit beyond the tax on income from personal exertion is lost or set against the tax on other income`

-- Version 0.5.0: row IL-02's fork F13 is a switch (its v0.4.0, SHRUG). The
-- capstone's reading maps to the row's: its default to the row's switch, which
-- declines where the value exceeds the tax; the pipeline's own default asks both
-- named readings and compares the tax (fork K23).
@ref ITO s 66(c)(1A), (4), (5) (row IL-02 v0.4.0, ito66-c-credit-points.l4; IL-02 fork F13)
GIVEN `the points for children` IS A NUMBER
      `the value`               IS A NUMBER
      `the tax`                 IS A NUMBER
      x                         IS AN `IL-07 a reading of the set-off of the children's credit under section 66(c)(4)-(5)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-02: the credit for` `the points for children` `children's points at a value of` `the value` `, set against a tax on income from personal exertion of` `the tax` `, reading the set-off as` x MEANS
    `s 66(c)(4)-(5) — the credit for children, set against the tax on income from personal exertion:` `the points for children` `,` `the value` `,` `the tax`
        `, reading the set-off as`
            (CONSIDER x
             WHEN `IL-07: the children's credit under section 66(c), declined where its reading changes the tax` THEN `section 66(c)(4)-(5) — the reading this row takes of the set-off of the children's credit`
             WHEN `IL-07: the children's credit capped at the tax on income from personal exertion`            THEN `the children's credit is capped at the tax on income from personal exertion`
             WHEN `IL-07: the children's credit set first against the tax on income from personal exertion`   THEN `the children's credit is set first against the tax on income from personal exertion`)

§§ `Subsections (a) and (b) — where the salary is assessed (a cross-check only)`

-- The pipeline takes the earner's taxable income to be the year's salary in every
-- case the capstone answers (NOTES.md fork K4). Where the earner is the spouse
-- who is not registered, IL-02 itself places that income in the separate
-- calculation, and the tests compare the two. Where the earner is the registered
-- spouse, IL-02 says s 65 governs and does not compute it (its assumption A3).
@ref ITO s 66(a), (b) (row IL-02, ito66-ab-taxable-income.l4)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`IL-02 reports that no separate calculation is made under section 66(a) for this couple` MEANS
    REFUSE "IL-02 reports that no separate calculation is made under section 66(a) for this couple"

@ref ITO s 66(a), (b) (row IL-02, ito66-ab-taxable-income.l4)
GIVEN h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      c IS AN `IL-07 couple`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-02: the taxable income in the separate calculation under section 66(a), in` h `married as` c MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 66(a)-(b) — the calculations, for` (`IL-02: the spouses in the tax year, in` h `married as` c)
    WHEN `a separate calculation is made under subsection (a)` `on the registered spouse` `in the separate calculation` `own (b)`
        THEN `in the separate calculation`
    OTHERWISE `IL-02 reports that no separate calculation is made under section 66(a) for this couple`
